The blend films of the most high-performance $P_{\mathsf{D}}$ and SMA materials are typically very brittle because of their rigid backbones with multiple fused rings. To address the issue, we designed a series of PM6- $b$ -PDMS BCP PDs by covalently linking two different blocks and achieving the desired nanostructures in the PSC film (Figure 1). We anticipated that this BCP design strategy can combine the advantages of the PM6 blocks (high photovoltaic performance) and the PDMS blocks (high stretchability). The PM6-bPDMS BCP $\rho_{\mathsf{D}}\mathsf{s}$ were synthesized by Stille coupling between the Sn-ended PM6 block and Br-ended PDMS block (Figure 1 and Scheme S1). Sn-ended PM6 block was synthesized by the Stille coupling between the monomers of (4,8-bis(5-(2-ethylhexyl)-4- fluorothiophen-2-yl)benzo[1,2-b:4,5-b']dithiophene-2,6-diyl)bis(trimethylstannane) (BDT-F, 1.1 equivalent) and 1,3-bis(5-bromothiophen-2-yl)-5,7-bis(2-ethylhexyl)benzo[1,2-c:4,5- c']dithiophene-4,8-dione (BDD, 1 eq)). The ratio between the BDT-F monomer and BDD
