We then evaluated cyclic durability of the IS-PSC devices by repetitively stretching the devices up to 100 cycles with a fixed strain of $15\%$ (Figure S22). The durability of the IS-PSCs based on PM6- $b_{\l}$ -PDMSx:L8-BO blends was significantly higher than those of the PM6:L8-BO binary or PM6:PDMS $\boldsymbol{12\mathrm{k}}$ :L8-BO ternary blends. For example, the IS-PSCs based on the PM6-b-PDMS $\displaystyle{12{\sf k}}$ :L8-BO retained $77\%$ of initial PCE after 100 times stretched. In contrast, the IS-PSCs based on PM6:L8-BO and PM6:PDMS $\boldsymbol{\mathsf{12k}}$ :L8-BO showed only 43 and $3\%,$ respectively, of their initial PCEs after the same numbers of stretching. Interestingly, for the PM6- $b$ -PDMSx:L8-BO blend-based IS-PSCs, the cyclic durability of the IS-PSCs was gradually enhanced by increasing the molecular weight of PDMS block in the BCPs. These results demonstrate that the mechanically robust active layers are crucial in constructing highly stretchable IS-PSCs.[3d,27b]
